  "registryUiItemsInIndex": 63,
  "stateMatrixCompleteness": "Good for core controls: Button has 7 variants (default, outline, secondary, ghost, destructive, link) x 8 sizes (default, xs, sm, lg, icon, icon-xs, icon-sm, icon-lg) with hover, aria-expanded, focus-visible ring, aria-invalid, disabled (opacity-50, pointer-events-none), loading handled by Spinner composition; light and dark class variants inline. Input/Select/Switch/Tabs/Badge/Card have size or variant axes (Card size sm/default, Switch size sm/default, Tabs variant default|line). No success/warning variants; no loading/skeleton state matrix; empty/error states left to Field/Empty. Each component ships in two primitive flavours (radix-* and base-* styles), 6 visual presets."
 },
 "tokenArchitecture": "Two layers + component classes. (1) CSS variables on :root/.dark: semantic surface/foreground pairs (background, card, popover, primary, secondary, muted, accent, destructive) + border/input/ring + chart-1..5 + sidebar-*, all oklch. (2) Tailwind v4 `@theme inline` maps them to --color-* utilities (bg-primary, text-muted-foreground) and derives the radius scale from --radius. No primitive colour ramps are shipped (palette is just 7 base-colour recipes). Component source is copied into the project (components.json: style=base-nova|radix-nova, tailwind.baseColor, cssVariables true) and styled with cva class strings using data-slot attributes. Presets are short codes (e.g. `a2r6bw`) decoded by `shadcn preset decode` and re-appliable with `shadcn apply <preset> --only theme|font`.",
 "distinctiveness": "Not a look but a distribution model: you own the code, tokens are tiny, and everything (CLI, registry, skills, MCP, presets, create page) is built for agents. The default look is intentionally near-monochrome so brand colour is the only decision. The 2026 six-preset axis (vega, nova, maia, lyra, mira, luma) shifts radius and density without changing the token API.",
 "weaknesses": [
  "No semantic status tokens (success, warning, info) in the default set",
  "No primitive colour ramps, so tints/hover shades are done with /80 opacity or color-mix, giving unpredictable contrast on tinted surfaces",
  "No documented contrast targets or type scale",
  "Default look is the most-copied SaaS style on the web; hard to differentiate",
  "Motion unspecified beyond class strings",
  "Component source drifts per project once copied (no upgrade path besides diff)",
  "Two primitive libraries (Radix vs Base UI) double the API surface"
 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "Name tokens as surface/foreground pairs (primary/primary-foreground) so any surface is guaranteed to have its readable text colour",
  "Derive the whole radius scale from one --radius multiplier ladder (0.6, 0.8, 1, 1.4, 1.8, 2.2, 2.6)",
  "Dark mode uses alpha borders (white 10%) and alpha input fills so borders work over any surface",
  "Give each state a ring-based focus recipe: 3px ring at 50% opacity plus border colour change; invalid state uses the same recipe in destructive",
  "Offer named presets (radius + density + font) as one short code instead of N free knobs",
  "Keep a size ladder per control (xs 24 / sm 28-32 / default 32-36 / lg 36-40) with icon-only siblings of equal square size",
  "Define extension protocol for new semantic tokens (:root, .dark, @theme inline) rather than hard-coding colours in components"
 ]
